it is a story we have been following all  day that crash happened off u.s  95 this morning south of boulder city we  do have team coverage tonight  joe mohler and the i-team's vanessa  murphy live tonight with reaction from  the cycling community  as well as safety tips for cyclists but  first let's begin with kristen  drummond who is live at the scene with  more on what exactly happened  kristen  [Music]  denise and brian the deadly crash  happening across the highway from me  here on u.s 95 south at around 9  30 this morning the location is about 15  miles north of  searchlight the southbound lanes were  shut down for  about six hours today troopers say about  10  cyclists were riding south when a white  box truck driving the same direction  went into their lane  now the reason why remains unknown right  now but impairment  is not suspected nhp confirms four men  and  one woman died three others were hurt  including one who was airlifted to umc  trauma  nhp says the cyclists on the ride were  familiar with the route and made this  trip before  a support and gear car also known as a  sag vehicle  also accompanied them until today's  tragedy they  they've never had any problems they  didn't have a safety vehicle with them  what i understand though is the safety  vehicle  ended up in a position where they were  bicyclists both in front of it  at the time of this crash  the driver of the sag car was  hospitalized  and hp says the box truck driver was not  hurt  and cooperated with troopers i'm told  that the cyclists who participated in  the group ride are all  advanced cyclists and this is all part  of a 130 mile  bike birthday ride
 

